  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -188,
        "title": "Microring modulator tuning — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "Laser LAS1 sits at a fixed 1309.9772 nm and feeds the",
          "microring RING1; the through port (prx) ends at TERM1.",
          "Tuning voltage VT1 sweeps -3 to 3 V, shifting the ring's",
          "resonance (electro-optic / carrier effect). As resonance",
          "crosses the laser line, prx drops into a deep notch, then",
          "recovers -- the classic ring tuning transmission curve.",
          "",
          "Set LAS1.wavelength_nm = 1310.5 and re-run to see the",
          "notch shift to a different tuning voltage."
        ]
      }
    ],
